Additionally, under the prompt corrective action requirements, which complement the capital conservation buffer, insured depository institutions are required to meet the following increased capital level requirements in order to qualify as “well capitalized”:
● a total risk-based capital ratio of 10.00% (unchanged from current rules);
● a Tier I risk-based capital ratio of 8.00% (increased from 6.00%);
● a new common equity Tier I risk-based capital ratio of 6.50%; and
● a Tier I leverage ratio of 5.00%.
